  "body": "Follow-up from #108 (branch issue/108-probe-ops).\n\nWhat happens: `operation::probe_op::stylus_hits` sweeps only the stylus BALL along every probe move against the model. The stylus shank above the ball and the probe body (the tool's `shank_*` band) are not judged, so a deep edge / corner / boss touch beside a taller wall, or a bore deeper than the stylus length, can pass while the shank or body meets the part.\n\nExpected: the shank (stylus length above the ball) and the probe body are swept like the cutter's shank bands in the reach laws; any meeting before the expected contact is a blocking warning, refused by name.\n\nDone means: a test with a touch whose ball clears but whose stylus shank or body meets a wall is refused; the clean fixtures stay clean.\n",
